          "block_index": 1,
          "component_id": "e49383c6-64b0-52ed-b0d9-d46f64e4b148",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 996,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:8.60.130:block:1",
          "start": 111
        },
        "quote": "Pursuant to TMC 8.75.040 , the Administrative Hearing Officer may order the owner of any premises upon which is located any structure, which after review is determined to be so deteriorated or dilapidated or has become so out of repair as to be dangerous, unsafe, insanitary or otherwise unfit for human habitation or occupancy, such that it is unreasonable to repair the structure, to: (1) demolish and remove such structure; or (2) if such structure is capable of being made safe by repairs, to repair and make safe and sanitary; or (3) to board up and hold for future repair; or (4) where there has been a cessation of normal construction of any structure for a period of more than two years, demolition and removal or boarding up for future repair. Boarding the structure up for future repair shall not extend beyond one year, unless approved by the Administrative Hearing Officer.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:8.60.130:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 8.60.130 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "fd3faa8c-00aa-5764-9842-03caceead71b",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1150,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:8.60.130:block:2",
          "start": 997
        },
        "quote": "“Unreasonable to repair” means that the repair costs exceed 30% of the replacement value of the structure as established by the Shawnee County Appraiser.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:8.60.130:block:2#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
